 "answer": "To re-run only the promptfoo test cases that ended in an error due to issues like network problems or rate limits, you can use the `promptfoo retry` command. Here's how you can do it:\n\n1. **Retry Errors from the Latest Eval:**\n   - Use the command `promptfoo eval --retry-errors`. This will automatically find ERROR results from the latest evaluation and re-run only those test cases. It's particularly useful when evals fail due to temporary network issues, rate limits, or API errors. If the retry fails, the original ERROR results are preserved, and you can safely run the command again.\n\n2. **Retry Errors from a Specific Eval:**\n   - Use the command `promptfoo retry <evalId>`. Replace `<evalId>` with the specific evaluation ID you want to target. This command finds test cases that resulted in errors and re-runs only those test cases, updating the results in place in the original evaluation.\n\n**Note:** The `--retry-errors` flag cannot be used together with `--resume` or `--no-write` flags.\n\nThese commands utilize the original evaluation's configuration and runtime options to ensure consistency.",
